WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.152 --> 00:00:02.510
(gentle bright music)

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.420
- People think fat people
never get off the couch

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.850
and people think that fat people
sit around eating all day.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.640
My mission is to challenge
people's assumptions

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.970
about fat people.

00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:25.280
(gentle piano music)

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.210
I'm Mirna Valerio, and I'm a runner.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.210
I've been running long
distance for about eight years.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.460
I've done nine marathons
and 10 ultra-marathons

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.280
with my longest being 100K.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.850
Traditionally, trail races
and other outdoor events

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.590
have not always been
welcoming to people like me.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.900
I'm black, I'm a woman, and I'm fat.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.320
When I go to a race, I
know I'm breaking the mold.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.260
It's still very white and very male.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.480
So I know going in that
I'm going to be different.

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:04.971
(soft piano music)

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.620
10 years ago I lived a very stressful life,

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.890
and so that took a huge toll on my health.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.760
I consulted with a doctor who told me

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.920
that I needed to change my
lifestyle pretty drastically

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.650
if I wanted to see my
son grow up, so I did.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.490
I'd had some experiences with people

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.880
always making the assumption
that whatever I was doing

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.220
it was for weight loss.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:38.800
After a couple of years,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.510
it was not a weight loss thing anymore;

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.820
it's about fitness.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.040
Running makes me feel like

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.580
my most human self.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.810
My first mile was pretty awful.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:57.360
It was painful, it was slow.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.180
When I'm feeling like this
is really too difficult,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.120
I know that in the end
I'm doing it for a reason.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.160
There's always a larger reason.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.010
The end goal not always
only being to finish,

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.550
but the more important
thing is that I'm out there

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:13.130
because sometimes I come in last.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.220
It's amazing to me how many messages I get

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.130
on a daily basis saying,

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.830
"Thank you for being you,

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.320
"thank you for living in your own space

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.400
"and taking up space, and
not being afraid to do that

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.400
"because that has allowed me to do that."

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.090
I'm gonna continue
doing it because I think

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.433
people still need to see me.

00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:35.183
(dramatic music)

00:02:39.696 --> 00:02:42.196
(chime dings)

